The data bundled in this repository is NOT MIT-licensed and carries its own
terms:

  data/species.json   A DERIVATIVE WORK of FishBase and SeaLifeBase, used under
                      CC-BY-NC 4.0 — attribution required, NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY.

                        Froese, R. and D. Pauly, eds. (2025). FishBase.
                        https://www.fishbase.org
                        Palomares, M.L.D. and D. Pauly, eds. (2025). SeaLifeBase.
                        https://www.sealifebase.org

                      Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

                      Changes made: filtered from 44,140 species to 539 (sharks
                      and cetaceans only); kept only depth range, habitat and
                      taxonomy; restructured. The day/night/dvm fields were ADDED
                      by us and are NOT FishBase data — see
                      data/species.SOURCES.md.

  data/basemap.png    Derived from the AWS Terrain Tiles open dataset
                      (GEBCO bathymetry, SRTM topography). Open.

  Occurrence records fetched at runtime from OBIS (https://obis.org) are CC-BY.
  Species text fetched at runtime from Wikipedia is CC-BY-SA.

If you intend to use this commercially, you must replace data/species.json with
a source that permits it. The depth range of every species in the app comes from
FishBase/SeaLifeBase.
